---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Capture from '../components/Capture.astro';
import { app } from '../config';
---
<Layout title="Ancrate — Your Notes. Your next steps." description="A Mac companion for Apple Notes. Bring your checklists together, focus on recent tasks, and use slash commands without leaving your notes. Coming soon.">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> A companion for Apple Notes · macOS 14+</p>
    <h1>Your Notes.<br />Your <span class="marked">next steps.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">Good ideas live in your notes. So do the things you meant to do.<br class="desktop-break" /> Ancrate brings your checklists together, so you can find what’s next.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#tour">Take a look <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/support/">Meet your Notes companion <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <div class="hero-preview"><Capture src="/images/all-todos.png" alt="Ancrate’s All to-dos view gathers open checklists from several sample Apple Notes, with completed filters and links back to the source notes." eager /><span class="preview-label">Your checklists. One clear view.</span></div>
    <p class="image-note">Actual app captures, using built-in sample notes.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="features" class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A little more clarity</p><h2>Keep the notes.<br />Find the next thing.</h2><p>You already have a place for your ideas. Ancrate helps you follow through on the checklists inside them.</p></div>
    <div class="features-grid">
      <article><span class="feature-number">01 / TOGETHER</span><h3>Less searching.<br />More doing.</h3><p>Gather tasks across your notes. See what’s open, what’s done, and which note each task came from. Check it off in Apple Notes; Ancrate reflects the change.</p><a class="text-link" href="#tour">Explore your lists <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></article>
      <article><span class="feature-number">02 / IN FOCUS</span><h3>Today’s work.<br />A wider view.</h3><p>Switch between all to-dos, the past month, and the past three months. Recent lists follow the source note’s date. Include the folders you want and leave individual notes out.</p><a class="text-link" href="/support/#sources">Choose your sources <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      <article><span class="feature-number">03 / AT HAND</span><h3>Small window.<br />Clear next step.</h3><p>A compact, pinnable panel stays beside your work. Open it from the menu bar, search by task, note, or folder, then jump straight to the original note.</p><a class="text-link" href="/support/#task-panel">Get to know the panel <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="tour" class="tour-section section">
    <div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">In your own rhythm</p><h2>A place for what comes next.</h2><p>A full view when you need perspective. A little panel when you just need the next task.</p></div>
      <div class="tour-grid"><figure><Capture src="/images/past-month.png" alt="The Past month view shows checklists from recently edited sample notes." /><figcaption><strong>Focus on what’s recent.</strong><span>Bring checklists from the past month into view.</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="panel-figure"><div class="panel-stage"><img src="/images/task-panel.png" alt="Ancrate’s floating task panel with search, date ranges, and tasks grouped by source note." width="642" height="888" loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption><strong>Keep your next steps nearby.</strong><span>Pin a compact panel beside Apple Notes.</span></figcaption></figure></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap commands-section">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">A shortcut to your flow</p><h2>A little slash.<br />A quicker start.</h2><p class="section-copy">Type <kbd>/</kbd> at the start of a line in Apple Notes. Choose a heading, checklist, quote, or table—right in the editor you already use.</p><p class="section-copy">Or use <code>/tasks</code>, <code>/month</code>, and <code>/quarter</code> to open your collected to-dos.</p><a class="text-link" href="/support/#slash-commands">Set up slash commands <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small-note">Optional. Requires Accessibility permission and Ancrate running.</p></div>
    <div class="command-stage"><span class="command-label">APPLE NOTES + ANCRATE</span><img src="/images/slash-menu.png" alt="Ancrate’s slash menu lists native Notes formatting options and commands for opening collected to-dos." width="600" height="718" loading="lazy" /><p>Choose with ↑ ↓ · Apply with Return or Tab</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap extras-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Made for your Mac</p><h2>Fits beside the way you work.</h2></div><div class="extras-grid"><article><span aria-hidden="true" class="extra-icon">▤</span><h3>A place on your desktop.</h3><p>Small, medium, and large widgets show a local snapshot of your to-dos. Keep Ancrate running for fresh updates; macOS controls when widgets redraw.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true" class="extra-icon">⌘</span><h3>Your tools, connected.</h3><p>Optional read-only MCP lets a local AI client list, search, and read notes and checklists. It cannot edit them. The client may send returned content to its provider.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true" class="extra-icon">◎</span><h3>Local by default.</h3><p>No Ancrate account, built-in analytics, or note uploads to an Ancrate server. Your notes are read on your Mac. <a href="/privacy/">Read the privacy details ↗</a></p></article></div></section>

  <section class="section video-section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Thirty seconds with Ancrate</p><h2>See it all come together.</h2></div><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/social.png" width="1920" height="1080" aria-label="Ancrate promotional preview with sample app captures and instrumental music"><source src="/images/ancrate-preview.mp4" type="video/mp4" />Your browser cannot play this video. <a href="/images/ancrate-preview.mp4">Download the Ancrate preview.</a></video><p class="image-note">A preview of tasks, source controls, search, and quick commands. <a href="/support/">Read the feature and setup guide.</a></p></section>

  <section id="availability" class="availability wrap"><img src="/icon.png" width="76" height="76" alt="" /><p class="eyebrow">Your Notes. Your next steps.</p><h2>{app.downloadUrl ? 'Make room for what’s next.' : 'A clearer view is coming.'}</h2><p>{app.downloadUrl ? 'Get Ancrate for your Mac.' : 'Ancrate is getting ready for release. A download link will appear here when it’s available.'}</p><a class="button primary" href={app.downloadUrl || `mailto:${app.supportEmail}?subject=Ancrate%20enquiry`}>{app.downloadUrl ? 'Get Ancrate' : 'Get in touch'} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small-note">Requires macOS 14 or later.</p></section>
</Layout>
